ent for a period of extramural practice under intelligent tutelage.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["functioning","working","utilitarian","functional","in working order","operational","running like a top","up"],"antonyms":["dysfunctional","non-functional","nonfunctional","unfunctional","organic","out of order"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["afunctional","amphifunctional","anatomofunctional","antifunctional","bifunctional","biofunctional","biofunctionalization","cofunctional","ecofunctional","eigenfunctional","equifunctional","eufunctional","functional beverage","functional constituency","functional drink","functional equivalence","functional graph","functionalise","functionalism","functionalist","functionalistic","functionality","functionalization","functionalize","functional linguistics","functional load","functionally","functional medicine","functional music","functional necrophilia"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/functional#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bcd21436599cc830f8","definition":"Optimized for all-around physiological benefit.","example":"functional coffee","pos":"adj","synonyms":["functioning","working","utilitarian","functional","in working order","operational","running like a top","up"],"antonyms":["dysfunctional","non-functional","nonfunctional","unfunctional","organic","out of order"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["afunctional","amphifunctional","anatomofunctional","antifunctional","bifunctional","biofunctional","biofunctionalization","cofunctional","ecofunctional","eigenfunctional","equifunctional","eufunctional","functional beverage","functional constituency","functional drink","functional equivalence","functional graph","functionalise","functionalism","functionalist","functionalistic","functionality","functionalization","functionalize","functional linguistics","functional load"